   <text>
      <body>
         <div n= "1" style="Callendar">
<!--For both calendars I wanted to describe the drawings that Mary Behrend did to the best that I coudld. I used <p> to include the notes
    that she put down on the paper.-->
            <note type="copyright">COPYRIGHT <date when="1908">1908, BY FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. NEW BRITAIN CONN.</date></note>
            <figure>
               <metamark> </metamark>
               <dateline>March 17, 1909. Wednesday, St. Patricks day </dateline>
               <figDesc>Stylised way of writing the date. Big green "m" for march to go along
                  with St. Paddy's. Snakes go around the date.</figDesc>
               <lg>
                  <l style="black">SAINT PATRICK WAS A USEFUL SAINT</l>
               <l>HE FREIGHTENED ALL THE SNAKES AWAY-</l>
               <l>I WISH HE'D TRY HIS ART ON THE<emph style="underlined">SMOKE</emph></l>
               <l>AROUND HAMMERMILL SOME DAY!</l>
               </lg>
               <figDesc>3-leaf clovers surrond the text and below said text is a rendetion of the
                  Hammermill factory. The building has a falt roofed part, then a sloped roof,then
                  two smokestacks that billow smoke, and finally one more flat roofed
                  area.</figDesc>
               <p style="red">The Hammermill <unclear reason="illegible"/>!</p>
            </figure>
         </div>
         <div n="2" style = "Callendar">
            <note type="copyright">COPYRIGHT <date when="1908">1908, BY FRIENDSHIP CALENDAR CO. NEW BRITAIN CONN.</date></note>
            <figure>
               <dateline>March 12, 1909. Friday</dateline>
               <figDesc>Stylised red "m" for March</figDesc>
               <p><persName>Molly</persName> on snowshoes That Mr. Weir Got. Pretty Picture Is it
                  Not?</p>
               <figDesc>A rendition of Marry Behrend with rosy cheeks, some sort of headwear,
                  gloves, a jacket, and massive cartoonish snow shoes.</figDesc>
               <p><unclear reason="illegible"></unclear></p>
            </figure>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
